							<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 0.5in; text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 24pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Rules and Regulations</span></strong><span style="font-family: &quot;Arial Unicode MS&quot;;"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 1in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Symbol;">·</span><span style="font-size: 7pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">General</span></strong></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 1in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Symbol;">·</span><span style="font-size: 7pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Raids</span></strong></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 1in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Symbol;">·</span><span style="font-size: 7pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Raid Loot Rules</span></strong></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 1in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Symbol;">·</span><span style="font-size: 7pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Events</span></strong></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 1in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Symbol;">·</span><span style="font-size: 7pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Dragon Kill Points</span></strong></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 1in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Symbol;">·</span><span style="font-size: 7pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Guild Removals</span></strong></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 1in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Symbol;">·</span><span style="font-size: 7pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">A Quick Overview of Terms</span></strong></p> <div class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 24pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue; font-weight: normal;"> <hr align="center" size="2" width="100%" /> </span></strong></div> <p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Verdana; color: red;">General</span></strong><strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"> </span></strong><span style="font-family: &quot;Arial Unicode MS&quot;;"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <ul style="margin-top: 0in;" type="disc"> <li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">No member, new or old shall run a casino or sell platinum or game cards on a guilded character.&nbsp; This is to protect our guild's good name.&nbsp; If you are selling your account, it is asked that you disband from the guild prior to the sale.</span><span style="font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">No member should apply to another guild without disbanding from MR first.</span><span style="font-family: Verdana;">&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Be respectful of everyone.&nbsp; This includes guild members as well as non-guild members.&nbsp; Remember the Golden Rule: Treat others the way you want to be treated.</span><span style="font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Don't kill steal (KS).&nbsp; It's against Everquest Rules, and it's rude.&nbsp; If someone else has first agro, let them have the mob.&nbsp; It's really not that big of a deal after all.</span><span style="font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Don't beg for items, money or leveling help.&nbsp; This gets annoying.&nbsp; Some people join a guild to just to get items, money or power leveling.&nbsp; To attempt to avoid this problem, new members cannot bid on items until they have been members of MR for 30 days.</span><span style="font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Don't go anonymous.&nbsp; Be proud of your guild, and let everyone know it!&nbsp; Role-play hides the zone you're in, your class and level, but still shows your guild name.</span><span style="font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Work on levels and Alternate Advancement skills all you want, but be willing to help fellow guild members too.&nbsp; Other people may not want to help you with that quest if you haven't been helping anyone else.</span><span style="font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Keep guild chat friendly.&nbsp; Cursing won't be tolerated in any guild-related chat channel.&nbsp; Everquest is a game, and should be enjoyed as such without offensive chatter.</span><span style="font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Don't hound anyone because you're not happy with the way they led a raid, group, or other event.&nbsp; Even at the highest level, we are all still learning and we all have feelings.&nbsp; If you have a serious problem, contact a guild officer.</span><span style="font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Unless otherwise stated, items in the guild bank are bid on with bid points (DKP).&nbsp; If you are interested in an item,&nbsp;find the item in the <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1085">Guild Bank</a> or <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1084">Spell Bank</a> page of the website.&nbsp;&nbsp;Post your opening bid on the Guild&nbsp;Bank forum.&nbsp; You may go no more than 10 DKP negative at any time.&nbsp; If you are already negative in DKP, then you may not bid on an item. </span><span style="font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Unclaimed Raid items will be kept in guild bank and listed on site. </span><o:p></o:p></li> </ul> <div class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 0.5in; text-align: center;" align="center"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"> <hr align="center" size="2" width="100%" /> </span></div> <p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Verdana; color: red;">Raids</span></strong><strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"> </span></strong><span style="font-family: &quot;Arial Unicode MS&quot;;"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <ul style="margin-top: 0in;" type="disc"> <li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Raids may be held anytime, although they should be held during the official guild raid times.&nbsp; Check <a href="/forums/threadlist.aspx?fid=1163">Raid Forums</a> on the website for upcoming raids.&nbsp; Check guild motd for details on each raid.&nbsp; To bring up the guild motd for quick viewing, type /get</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">No raid is mandatory, however everyone should be willing to help out the guild with raids whenever possible.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Follow the directions given by your raid or group leader.&nbsp; It's when people don't listen that a whole raid wipes and everyone dies.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Keep the raid channel clear of non-raid related chatter.&nbsp; When people chat in raid channels, it becomes difficult to pay attentions to the raid instructions</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">If you need a raid for an item that you want, make a post in the “<a href="/forums/threadlist.aspx?fid=1163">Raids</a>“ forum on the site.&nbsp; The raid officer will coordinate a date and time for the raid, and announce it in guild motd and post it on the guild calendar.&nbsp; </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">During raids try to control your tempers, but try not to take offense to anything that may be said.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>Tempers run wild during raids sometimes, and its important to remember this and try to control it. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Keep role-play on during raids.&nbsp; Don't tell anyone outside of the guild about the raid, (even if you're not on the raid) until the raid is over.&nbsp; Other guilds will try to steal raids on occasion, so keep it quiet. </span><o:p></o:p></li> </ul> <div class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 0.5in; text-align: center;" align="center"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"> <hr align="center" size="2" width="100%" /> </span></div> <p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 0.5in;">&nbsp;<span style="font-family: &quot;Arial Unicode MS&quot;;"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 0.5in; text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Verdana; color: red;">Raid Loot Rules</span></strong></p> <ul style="margin-top: 0in;" type="disc"> <li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">There will be up to 1 looter per group.&nbsp; Any no drop items will be bid on right away, while other items are bid on directly after the raid. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">When bidding opens on an item, it is only open to full members that can use it right away. *&nbsp; If no character can use nor wants it, bidding then becomes open to probationary members, if no probationary member wants it or can use it, then bidding is open to alts.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Any platinum&nbsp;will be added to the <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1085">guild's&nbsp;bank</a>, and any leftover items will be added to the <a href="../item_view.aspx">guild's raid bank</a>.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Guild bank platinum will be used to help cover components used during raids, or for guild events, and nobody may bid on guild platinum.&nbsp; Any components given to you during a raid are to be used for the raid only.&nbsp; Any leftover items can be given back to the bank or used for a future raid.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Raid loot decisions are final.&nbsp; If you're not happy with something, bring it up privately with an officer. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">*If a player is on an alt during a raid, he/she will have the option to bid for items on one of the following: the current alt they're playing, or their main character.&nbsp; This does not include no drop items.&nbsp; If you decide to bid on items for your main character you need to tell the raid leader before the raid begins.&nbsp; It is up to the raid leader to decide if he/she wishes to allow you to do this.&nbsp; If you are doing this then you can only bid on items for one character.&nbsp; You may NOT bid on items for both characters.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Raid leaders are responsible for dumping the raid file and sending it to the site email address.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>This is to ensure that members receive any DKP they’ve earned.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>If at any time you didn’t receive the points you earned, email the site and we’ll investigate it and update it if necessary.</span><o:p></o:p></li> </ul> <div class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 0.5in; text-align: center;" align="center"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"> <hr align="center" size="2" width="100%" /> </span></div> <p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in; text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Verdana; color: red;">Dragon Kill Points (DKP)</span></strong></p> <ul style="margin-top: 0in;" type="disc"> <li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">For attending a raid you generally will receive approximately 1 DKP per hour, however certain targets may earn more or less DKP.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">DKP are used for bidding on raid items or items in the <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1084">Guild's Spell Bank</a> or <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1085">Guild bank</a> </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">For hosting a guild power-level event 1&nbsp;DKP per hour. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Attending a guild event you receive 2&nbsp;DKP per event. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Hosting a guild event you receive 5&nbsp;DKP per event.&nbsp; </span></li> </ul> <div class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 0.5in; text-align: center;" align="center"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"> <hr align="center" size="2" width="100%" /> </span></div> <p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Verdana; color: red;">Events</span></strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"> </span><span style="font-family: &quot;Arial Unicode MS&quot;;"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <ul style="margin-top: 0in;" type="disc"> <li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Ideally, guild events will be held monthly.&nbsp; Most likely on a weekend evening.&nbsp; No raids will be scheduled on the same night as an event.&nbsp; Guild events will be announced in the motd as well as the <a href="../calendar.aspx">calendar</a> and the Guild Forum.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Event prizes are wonderful, but not absolutely necessary.&nbsp; However, feel free to donate to the guild bank for prizes.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Events can be held by anyone.&nbsp; Contact an officer if you would like to host an event.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="color: blue;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">Generally, guild events are limited to guild members only.&nbsp; However, it is possible for others to attend an event with the permission of the event's host. </span><o:p></o:p></li> </ul> <div class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"> <hr align="center" size="2" width="100%" /> </span></div> <p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Verdana; color: red;">Guild Removals </span></strong><span style="font-family: &quot;Arial Unicode MS&quot;;"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <ul style="margin-top: 0in;" type="disc"> <li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">We work on a "3 strikes and you're out" policy.&nbsp; A warning is given for the first infraction.&nbsp; The second offense puts you on probation, while the third offense gets you disbanded.&nbsp; You will be notified via email of any offense.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Any verified reports of scamming will result in the member being disbanded.&nbsp; Play fair!</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Any character that is inactive for 6 weeks or more will be disbanded.&nbsp; If you suspect you will be away for 6 weeks or more, contact the guild leader to avoid being disbanded.&nbsp; This does not apply to alts.&nbsp; You will be notified via email 1 week prior to removal.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><ul style="margin-top: 0in;" type="circle"><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Officers will be demoted to member status if they are inactive for 3 weeks without prior notice, at which point they will be treated as members and given 6 weeks to return</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">If you contact the guild leader prior to leaving, this can be avoided.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Officers, prior to the actual removal of any member, will discuss the matter.&nbsp; However, there are some offenses that require immediate removal, including but not limited to:</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><ul style="margin-top: 0in;" type="circle"><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Racism</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Sexism</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Extremely offensive language</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Extreme disrespect of any guild member </span></li></ul> </ul> <div class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 1in; text-align: center;" align="center"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"> <hr align="center" size="2" width="100%" /> </span></div> <p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Verdana; color: red;">A Quick overview of Terms: </span></strong><span style="font-family: &quot;Arial Unicode MS&quot;;"><o:p></o:p></span></p> <ul style="margin-top: 0in;" type="disc"> <li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Motd is the message of the day.&nbsp; The motd is located in the guild manager and can be accessed by either hitting Alt G or by typing /get</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Alt is any character that is not a main character of the player.</span></li> </ul> <p class="MsoNormal"><a href="../custom.aspx?pid=1035">&nbsp;Back to Top</a></p> 
							
